<Base
  title="Privacy: MaKeeb"
  description="What the MaKeeb keyboard does with what you type: it stays on your phone."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p class="lead">
      MaKeeb is a keyboard, so it sees everything you type. It keeps all of it on your phone: nothing you type is sent
      anywhere, and the keyboard never uses the network.
    </p>

    <h2>What you type</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Text you type is handled on the phone and never leaves it. It is not logged, stored for later or uploaded.</li>
      <li>Suggestions, autocorrect and next-word predictions come from dictionaries on the phone.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Words MaKeeb learns</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        New words you type, such as names, are remembered so they can be suggested. They are stored only in the keyboard’s
        own storage on your phone and are left out of backups.
      </li>
      <li>
        Nothing is learned in password fields, in incognito mode, or in fields that turn off autocorrect (such as user names
        and e-mail addresses).
      </li>
      <li>
        You can forget a word by holding it in the suggestion strip. On Android, Settings → Learned words lists them, and
        removes one or all. On iOS, Settings → Learned words clears them.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Clipboard</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Recent clips are kept on the phone for the clipboard panel, and expire. Pinned clips and snippets stay until you remove them.</li>
      <li>Text a password manager copies as sensitive is never kept, and nothing is kept while incognito mode is on.</li>
      <li>On iOS, the clipboard panel needs Full Access. Typing works fully without it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Network</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The keyboard never uses the network. It types, corrects and predicts fully offline.</li>
      <li>
        The MaKeeb app goes online only when you download a dictionary for a language, during setup or in Settings.
        Dictionaries are downloaded from GitHub, which sees your IP address and which language you download, under{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
        Every download is checked against its published checksum before the keyboard uses it.
      </li>
      <li>There are no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no tracking.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>iOS Full Access</h2>
    <p>
      iOS asks whether to allow a keyboard “Full Access”. MaKeeb works fully without it. With it, MaKeeb can also show your
      clipboard, play haptics and click sounds, and save changes made in the keyboard’s quick settings. Full Access does not
      make MaKeeb send anything you type anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Android permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Vibration</strong>, for key feedback.</li>
      <li><strong>Internet</strong>, used only by the app to download dictionaries when you ask. The keyboard never uses it.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>

